  "decision": "HOLD",
  "fix_description": "Both findings are low-risk false positives or documentation-only items. (1) The subprocess.run calls at lines 6 and 14 already use shell=False and pass command arguments as lists, so there is no shell-string injection surface. A safe hardening option is to add an explicit comment and keep the list-form invocation; no behavioral code change is required. (2) The CI_TOKEN handling in run_fixture_tests removes the token from the subprocess environment and does not log or transmit it, so credential handling is normalized correctly. A minimal, safe fix is to add a clarifying comment that the environment is scrubbed before test execution and to avoid printing any environment or command output that could expose credentials. These changes are cosmetic and do not alter runtime behavior, so they can be applied as L0 documentation hardening.",
